{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 12 that avoid forbidden substrings \"111\" and \"000\". Count sequences with no three consecutive same bits. Classic Fibonacci-like. Count number of binary strings of length n with no run of 3 same bits. Let a_n be count. Recurrence: a_n = a_{n-1} + a_{n-2}. Actually for binary with no 3 consecutive same, we can use DP with states: last run length and last bit. Let's compute quickly.\n\nLet dp[n][b][k] where b=0/1 last bit, k=1 or 2 length of run. For n=1: dp[1][0][1]=1, dp[1][1][1]=1. For n>1: transition: if add same bit, only if k=1 then new k=2; if k=2 cannot add same. If add opposite bit, new k=1.\n\nWe can compute iteratively for n=12.\n\nLet's code mentally.\n\nInitialize counts for n=1:\nc01=1 (last 0 run1)\nc11=1 (last1 run1)\nAlso we can keep c02=0, c12=0.\n\nn=2:\nCompute new:\nFrom c01 (0 run1): add 0 -> run2: c02 +=1. add 1 -> run1: c11 +=1.\nFrom c11: add 1 -> run2: c12 +=1. add 0 -> run1: c01 +=1.\n\nSo after n=2:\nc01=1 (from c11)\nc02=1 (from c01)\nc11=1 (from c01)\nc12=1 (from c11)\n\nn=3:\nFrom c01 (0 run1): add 0 -> c02 +=1; add1 -> c11 +=1.\nFrom c02 (0 run2): cannot add 0; add1 -> c11 +=1.\nFrom c11 (1 run1): add1 -> c12 +=1; add0 -> c01 +=1.\nFrom c12 (1 run2): cannot add1; add0 -> c01 +=1.\n\nCompute totals:\nc01 new = from c11 + from c12 =1+1=2\nc02 new = from c01 =1\nc11 new = from c01 + from c02 =1+1=2\nc12 new = from c11 =1\n\nn=4:\nFrom c01 (0 run1): add0 -> c02 +=2; add1 -> c11 +=2.\nFrom c02 (0 run2): add1 -> c11 +=1.\nFrom c11 (1 run1): add1 -> c12 +=2; add0 -> c01 +=2.\nFrom c12 (1 run2): add0 -> c01 +=1.\n\nTotals:\nc01 = from c11 + from c12 =2+1=3\nc02 = from c01 =2\nc11 = from c01 + from c02 =2+1=3\nc12 = from c11 =2\n\nn=5:\nFrom c01 (0 run1): add0 -> c02 +=3; add1 -> c11 +=3.\nFrom c02 (0 run2): add1 -> c11 +=2.\nFrom c11 (1 run1): add1 -> c12 +=3; add0 -> c01 +=3.\nFrom c12 (1 run2):